{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (ticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 18 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the store / snapshot / io subsystem (_store, _snapshot, _io) as entries in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`. RP-04 is not complete while these ambient reads sit below the approved composition/credential/backend seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nAffected files (relative to repo root):\n  - `src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/ensures.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/lock.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_store/push.py`\n  - `src/rebar/config.py` (may add/reuse owned composition-root resolvers for the cut reads)\n  - `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the 18 drained rows)\n\n## Outcome\nEvery one of the 18 below-seam reads is dispositioned by the decision rule below into exactly one of two treatments, and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entry is removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths with those entries gone and no path-glob exception. The subsystem's behavioral suites stay green; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except recorded, justified deltas (recorded as a comment on this ticket).\n\n## Decision rule (which treatment each read gets)\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; the large majority).** A read whose value is composed configuration (a typed `Config` field or a `[snapshot]`/`sync`/`ensure`/`jira` table key, or `load_config()`) is CUT: the value is threaded from the composition seam — an owned `config.py` resolver (e.g. the existing `compose_config()` added by C3e, or a targeted owned resolver) — rather than read from ambient `os.environ`/`load_config` below the seam. No `# read-via:` marker; the ambient read no longer exists in the consumer.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed configuration — a genuine test-only injection point, a subsystem kill-switch, or a subprocess/protocol env-control — stays in place carrying a `# read-via:` marker whose rationale names the category. This branch is CAPPED at the 3 enumerated reads below; no other read in the listed paths may be marked-owned.\n\n### Enumerated owned-in-place allowlist (exactly 3 — the cap)\n1. `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py` :: `REBAR_HLC` — subsystem kill-switch (default-on; `REBAR_HLC=0` reverts the HLC clock to raw `physical_now()`). Not composed config; a staging kill-switch.\n2. `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py` :: `REBAR_HLC_NOW` — test-only injection of the physical clock source for the skewed-clock tests. Not composed config; a test control.\n3. `src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py` :: `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` — save/restore of the prior value around a deliberate child-process env mutation (the importer SETS `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` for subprocesses and restores the prior value). Not a config read; subprocess/protocol env-control.\n\nAll 15 other listed reads (the 3 `load_config()` calls; `REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_*` x3; `REBAR_GATE_*` x6 incl. the janitor dynamic `os.environ.get`; `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`; `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`; `REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY`) are treatment (a), cut-to-seam.\n\n## Plan\n1. Cut the 15 composed-config reads to the seam: thread each value from an owned `config.py` resolver (reuse `compose_config()` where a full `Config` is needed; add a small owned resolver only where a narrower typed value is cleaner), changing below-seam helper signatures to RECEIVE the composed value instead of reading ambient env/`load_config`. Preserve exact resolution semantics (env>config-table>default precedence for the `[snapshot]` knobs; clamping for `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`).\n2. Mark the 3 enumerated owned-in-place reads with a `# read-via:` marker carrying the category rationale; make no other markers in the listed paths.\n3. Remove the 18 corresponding entries for these files from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`.\n4. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration store/snapshot suites); keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Held-out test `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts:\n  (i) `check_config_ownership.check(check_config_ownership.REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding string containing any of the listed paths;\n  (ii) `config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` contains zero entries whose `path` is one of the listed files; AND\n  (iii) the number of `# read-via:` markers across the listed source files is exactly 3 (the enumerated cap) and each sits on one of the 3 allowlisted reads — so an executor cannot blanket-mark reads to pass instead of cutting them.\n  RED now (entries present + reads below seam + no markers).\n- The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration store/snapshot suites) stay green after the cutover — they are the correctness oracle the AST gate supplements.\n- Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after are equal except deltas recorded (with rationale) as a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored ticket/event/binding format changes. Cut-to-seam is a pure routing/threading change; the 3 markers are inline annotations. Rollback is reverting the single change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the approved seam in the 10 listed source files: each read is either cut-to-seam (15) or one of the exactly-3 enumerated owned-in-place reads carrying a `# read-via:` marker with a category rationale; no other read is marked-owned.\n- [ ] The 18 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries for these files are removed from `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`, and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out `test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py`, incl. its `# read-via:` marker-count == 3 cap check).\n- [ ] The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration store/snapshot suites) pass after the cutover; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except deltas recorded with rationale as a comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787104820589906001,"uuid":"98b4452e-25bd-43f5-9577-91f77dfe4853"}